  "description": "A parametric FLOOR DRAIN on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nIT SITS BELOW ZERO, which is the whole point. The frame and grating run from −frame depth up to 0, so the drain is recessed into the floor rather than standing on it, and a section through the bathroom shows the gully where it belongs.\n\nTHE FALL ZONE IS THE USEFUL PART. A drain on its own says nothing about whether the floor drains to it; the published fall zone — a 32-point circle at the fall radius, on its own slot and its own pale colour — is the region the screed has to slope toward. Switch it off for a clean drawing, leave it on while setting out.\n\nTHE GRATING IS A COUNTED LOOP: N slots across the clear opening at half-pitch spacing, so a 100 mm gully with five slots and a 200 mm one with ten both come out right, and the published open area is the number that decides flow rate.",
